# E212 Draft — Shell script interactive read blocks non-interactive execution
# Contributor: D2CC
# Created: 2026-07-02
# Software: lynis 3.1.7

title: Shell script interactive read blocks non-interactive execution
category: L2
severity: yellow
build_system: shell
step: smoke_test|test_package

error_signature: read -r void|Press ENTER to continue|Security check failed|hangs indefinitely|timeout kills

match_keywords: interactive,read,blocking,non-interactive,smoke_test,timeout,shell_script,ENTER,security_check

root_cause: |
  Shell scripts with interactive prompts (e.g., security checks asking user to press ENTER)
  block indefinitely when run in non-interactive environments such as conan test_package,
  CI pipelines, or L2 smoke tests. The `read` command waits for stdin input that never
  arrives, causing the process to hang until killed by timeout.
  This is common in security auditing tools (lynis, rkhunter, etc.) that have interactive
  security confirmation prompts.

affected_scope: |
  Any shell script tool with interactive prompts (read command waiting for user input).
  Known affected: lynis 3.1.7, potentially rkhunter, chkrootkit, and similar tools.

rec_description: |
  Three approaches (use any one):
  1. Make read non-blocking: replace `read -r var` with `read -r var < /dev/null 2>/dev/null || true`
  2. Add early argument handling before interactive checks:
     `for arg in "$@"; do case "$arg" in --version|-V) echo "$VERSION"; exit 0;; esac; done`
  3. Check terminal before prompting: `[ -t 0 ] && read -r var || true`
  Best practice: combine approaches 1 and 2 for robustness.

rec_command: sed -i 's/read -r void/read -r void < \/dev\/null 2>\/dev\/null || true/' script.sh

verification_cmd: timeout 10 ./script.sh --version && echo "PASS" || echo "FAIL"

rec_priority: medium

related_entries: E165
